      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, adopted your suggestion. The check now lives at the end of _ResolveSmartSyncOption, after the manifest default has been folded into opt.smart_sync, and the test at :199 now expects SmartSyncError.\n\nI also reworded the message, since -s/-t are no longer the only ways to end up smart syncing: \"-u and -p may only be used when smart syncing: pass -s or -t, or use a manifest with sync-smartsync\u003dtrue\".\n\nOne consequence worth calling out: this diagnostic used to come from OptionParser.error at parse time, so it printed usage and exited 2. It is now a SmartSyncError raised partway through _ExecuteHelper, after manifest.Override() and GetSmartSyncOverridePath() have already run. That seems unavoidable if the check has to see the manifest-resolved value of smart_sync, but the exit code and output format do change for this case. Happy to move it back to a usage error if you would rather keep that, at the cost of it not accounting for the manifest default.",
